  "description": "Outgoing messages to the places people read, without a vendor SDK: Discord and Slack webhooks, ntfy, and signed outgoing webhooks (Standard Webhooks). One message shape, a request per destination with agent-written text escaped for it, a check of each destination's address, and one reading of the answer: sent, retry after, gone, or failed, with a retry schedule. The host keeps its tables, its queue and when to send.",
